# $project_name

A LangGraph agent served by Zorvex, a self-hosted server for the LangSmith Deployment Agent Server API.

## Run it

```bash
uv sync
uv run zorvex dev
```

`zorvex dev` starts PostgreSQL with Docker or Podman, then serves the graph on <http://127.0.0.1:2026>, reloading on
code changes; the API reference is at <http://127.0.0.1:2026/docs>. Its first run creates `.env` from `.env.example`:
put your model provider's key there (`OPENAI_API_KEY` for `openai/...` models) and start it again.

`uv run zorvex up --wait` runs it all in containers instead: PostgreSQL, Redis and the server, built from the
`Dockerfile`.

## The model

The model is `provider/model`: `openai/gpt-4o-mini`, unless `MODEL` in `.env` or a run's context names another
(`src/$slug/context.py`). Only the first slash separates the two, so `openai/deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V3` asks provider
`openai` for the model `deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V3`. Set `OPENAI_BASE_URL` to have an OpenAI-compatible gateway serve
`openai/...` models.

## Layout

- `zorvex.json`: the graphs Zorvex serves
- `src/$slug/`: `graph.py` and the modules it imports
- `.env.example`: what `.env` starts from
- `docker-compose.yml`, `Dockerfile`: PostgreSQL, Redis and the server, for `zorvex up`
